<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Triarchy of Negroponte</h1><p class="st-meta">1205 CE – 1390 CE (approx.) · capital Negroponte</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Crusader lordship on Euboea, split among three Lombard lords under the growing shadow of Venice, which eventually took over the whole island.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat">Boniface of Montferrat</a> granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Euboea</a> in 1205 to Jacques d'Avesnes and then to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> nobles from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a>, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ravano-dalle-carceri">Ravano dalle Carceri</a>. In 1209 Ravano recognised Venetian overlordship. After his death in 1216 the island was divided into three parts, the terzieri, each held by a lord called a triarch.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The triarchs, of families such as the dalle Carceri and Ghisi, were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea</a> but relied on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, which held quarters and a bailo in the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Negroponte</a> (<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chalcis">Chalcis</a>) and controlled its trade. Greek peasants worked the land under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> lords. The renegade knight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licario">Licario</a>, serving <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>, recaptured much of the island in the 1270s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Threatened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-company">Catalans</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-athens">Duchy of Athens</a> and the Turks, the triarchs ceded more and more to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. By 1390 Venice ruled the whole island directly as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/venetian-negroponte">Venetian Negroponte</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/triarchy-of-negroponte.jpg" alt="Triarchy of Negroponte" width="320" height="183"><figcaption>Image: Cplakidas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greece_in_1210.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1205 CE – 1390 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Negroponte</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ravano dalle Carceri</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (population)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lordship of Negroponte, Triarchy of Euboea</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1298&amp;focus=triarchy-of-negroponte" aria-label="Triarchy of Negroponte on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5266 797 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Triarchy of Negroponte lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5586 1053L5530 1071M5586 1053L5293 831M5586 1053L5586 1053"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5530 1071h0M5293 831h0M5586 1053h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5586 1053h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5586 1053h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1298&amp;focus=triarchy-of-negroponte">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
